  m_Script: {fileID: 11500000, guid: 94872708bfe9e4851981e9e1837f1ac3, type: 3}
  m_Name: Sword
  m_EditorClassIdentifier: 
  exhibitName: The Sword of Victory
  description: 'The Sword was ceremonially gifted to the Tula state arms museum in
    Tula, Russia on 7th May 2015 marking the 70th anniversary of the victory in Great
    Patriotic War (WWII). It is one of several made in the Zlatoust arms factory
    and ceremonially gifted to various "Hero Cities" of the Soviet Union. The sword
    is hand-made from famous Zlatoust steel. It is 120 cm (about 47 inches) long,
    weighs over five kilograms, and is decorated with floral ornaments. One side
    of the blade features an inscription specific to Tula while the other side bears
    a quotation attributed to Alexander Nevsky: "Who with a sword will come to us,
    he will die by the sword".'
  images: []
